{"est_no":"167-31315","est_id":"8616","name":"Douglas Alternative School","est_type":"School","address":"444 W Reynolds","city":"Springfield","state":"IL","zip":"62702","visits":[{"id":"766297","date":"2026-05-28","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8616&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=766297&INSPECTION_NN=766297","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"610627","date":"2026-02-27","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":1,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"Minor issues","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8616&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=610627&INSPECTION_NN=610627","fetched":true,"findings":[{"item":10,"title":"Adequate handwashing sinks properly supplied and accessible.","repeat":false,"comment":"Upon arrival, the handwashing sink was observed obstructed with a cooking pan and dishes. The cooking equipment was removed from the sink to correct the violation. Given that the handwashing sink is used by multiple parties, the kitchen employee is responsible for keeping the sink free of dishes and unobstructed for handwashing purposes. Ensure that handsinks are always available for employees to wash hands.","citation":"5-205.11","citation_text":"5-205.11 Using a Handwashing Sink. (A) A HANDWASHING SINK shall be maintained so that it is accessible at all times for EMPLOYEE use. (B) A HANDWASHING SINK may not be used for purposes other than handwashing. (C) An automatic handwashing facility shall be used in accordance with manufacturer’s instructions."}]},{"id":"547468","date":"2025-05-27","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8616&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=547468&INSPECTION_NN=547468","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"537687","date":"2025-03-13","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8616&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=537687&INSPECTION_NN=537687","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"502680","date":"2024-05-20","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8616&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=502680&INSPECTION_NN=502680","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"476722","date":"2023-10-06","visit":"Follow-up","type_raw":"1st Re-Inspect","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8616&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=476722&INSPECTION_NN=476722","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"475290","date":"2023-09-26","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":2,"repeat":0,"grp":1,"label":"Minor issues","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8616&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=475290&INSPECTION_NN=475290","fetched":true,"findings":[{"item":1,"title":"Charge present, demonstrates knowledge, and performs duties","repeat":false,"comment":"","citation":"2-102.11","citation_text":"2-102.11 (A), (B) & (C)(1), (4)-(16) Priority violation was observed for hot and cold foods not received at proper temperature. Digital probe food thermometers were also not working to allow PIC the ability to confirm temperatures. Food temperatures could not be checked if inspector was not on-site today. Active managerial controls were discussed and will be revisited at follow-up inspection.\nBased on the risks inherent to the food operation, during inspections and upon request the PIC shall demonstrate to the regulatory authority knowledge of foodborne disease prevention, application of the hazard analysis and critical control points, and the requirements of the Code."},{"item":12,"title":"Food received at proper temperature","repeat":false,"comment":"","citation":"3-202.11","citation_text":"3-202.11 (A) & (D) 1. Mexican corn was observed with internal temperature of 125F. PIC stated they transported foods and arrived at the school within a few minutes prior to inspector’s arrival. Cook temperature for corn was documented as 165.9F. Best practices and proper heating of TCS foods were discussed. Ensure all TCS foods are heated to proper cook temperature prior to transport and arrive for service at proper hot holding temperature of 135F/above. All hot foods will be served or discarded by the end of lunch service. \n2. Portioned cheese shreds were observed with internal temperatures of 50F. PIC noted product was removed from a cooler holding at 34F prior to portioning this morning. Ensure cold TCS foods are immediately placed in cold holding after prep to chill product prior to transport, and transport cold TCS foods well packed with ice blankets so they arrive for service at proper cold holding temperature of 41F/below. All portions of cheese shreds were served during lunch period.\nExcept as specified in (B) of this section, refrigerated, time/temperature control for safety food shall be at a temperature of 41F/below when received. Time/temperature control for safety food that is cooked to a tempature and for a time specified under §§ 3-401.11 - 3-401.13 and received hot shall be at a temperature of 135F/above."},{"item":36,"title":"Thermometers provided & accurate","repeat":false,"comment":"","citation":"4-203.11","citation_text":"4-203.11 Digital probe food thermometers were not working at the time of inspection. PIC stated thermometers were working the day prior but batteries were getting low. New batteries will be provided for said thermometers to allow for use. Consider maintaining extra batteries at this location and/or bimetallic stem thermometers that register 0F-220F and do not require batteries as backup in addition to digital probe food thermometers. \nFood temperature measuring devices that are scaled only in Fahrenheit shall be accurate to ±2°F in the intended range of use."}]},{"id":"445060","date":"2023-02-01","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8616&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=445060&INSPECTION_NN=445060","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"436567","date":"2022-11-02","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8616&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=436567&INSPECTION_NN=436567","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"417014","date":"2022-05-02","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8616&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=417014&INSPECTION_NN=417014","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"402517","date":"2021-11-19","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8616&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=402517&INSPECTION_NN=402517","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"385046","date":"2021-05-04","visit":"Spot check","type_raw":"Spot Check","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No i